### To Reproduce

The following code snippet works perfectly fine in better-auth 1.4.6

```
plugins: [
        emailOTP({
            async sendVerificationOTP({ email, otp}) {
                const user = await db.user.findUnique({
                    where: { email },
                    select: { name: true, emailVerified: true },
                });

                if (!user) {
                    throw new APIError("BAD_REQUEST", {
                        message: "USER_NOT_FOUND", // This gets converted to error.code in the client. 
                    });
                }
```

Since better-auth 1.4.7 an the APIError thrown is Caught by Task Runner; logs "Failed to run background task". And on the client side, it returns a success message, so the following result.error no longer runs. 

```
 const result = await authClient.emailOtp.sendVerificationOtp({
                    email: _email,
                    type: "sign-in",
                });
                if (result.error) {
                    // if (result.error.code === authClient.$ERROR_CODES.USER_NOT_FOUND) {
                    if (result.error.code === "USER_NOT_FOUND") {
                        onRegisterCallback(_email);
                    }
```

Is this is the intended OTP behaviour? 
If so, what is the new workaround? 

### Current vs. Expected behavior

Current behaviour returns a success message with no errors. 

Expected behaviour should return the USER_NOT_FOUND error response

